Generic analysis:

Functions:

# Searching
Telecoms.peak_search(x)(x, y)
Search for the highest value in x with the result as (value, index).
(x, idx) or (x, y) if y given.

Telecoms.n_peak_search(x, n)(x, y, n)
Search for the first n highest peaks. Returns vector of the above
data. Prevent neighbouring peaks by specifying kwarg "backoff",
the number of indices between detected peaks. 

Telecoms.find(x, x_0)(x, y, y_0)
Find the point x_0 in x as (x, idx) or y_0 in y as (x, y).

Telecoms.data_around_peak(x, y, Dx)
Return a slice of x and y around the highest y value with Dx being
the slice size in +/- Dx.

Telecoms.data_around_trough(x, y, Dx)

# Calculating
Telecoms.dBm2mW(x)
mW2dBm

integral_from_module(t, x)
Integrate x along t

integral_rect
Integrate x along t using Riemann method

integral_trap
Integrate x along t using a trapezoidal method

# Checking
Telecoms.any_zero_nan(x)
Shorthand to check before logarithms.

# Discrete manipulation
Telecoms.undersample(x, factor)
Where factor is an integer, undersample uniformly at a ratio of
factor.

decimation_avg(t, x, factor)
Where factor is an integer, undersample uniformly at a ratio of
factor where the resulting sample is the mean of the discarded samples.
Useful for changing VBW when plotting.
